---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, PHONE_DISPLAY } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service | LeadVault"
  description="The terms that govern use of leadvaultdata.com and LeadVault's prospect intelligence, data, list cleaning, outreach, and trade-desk services."
  path="/terms-of-service"
  heading="Terms of Service"
  lastUpdated="August 15, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of <strong>leadvaultdata.com</strong> and any
    service you order from LeadVault — qualified prospect data, prospect intelligence, market &amp;
    ICP research, decision-maker intelligence, email list cleaning, intelligence-led outreach,
    Trade Desk buyer–seller matching, recurring prospect research, custom data projects, and data
    strategy consultations. By submitting our survey, placing an order, or using this site, you
    agree to these Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Our Services</h2>
  <p>
    LeadVault sources, verifies, and delivers business contact data and related services on
    request. Every engagement starts with a free recommendation (typically within 24 hours of your
    survey submission) describing the data or service we recommend, the expected volume, and the
    price — nothing is charged until you approve a quote.
  </p>

  <h2>Ordering &amp; Payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Pricing is quoted in USD unless otherwise agreed in writing.</li>
    <li>Custom data projects require a 50% deposit to begin work, with the balance due on delivery.</li>
    <li>Monthly subscriptions renew automatically each billing cycle until cancelled; see "Cancellation" below.</li>
    <li>Delivery timelines quoted (e.g. "3–5 days") are estimates based on the complexity of your specification, not guarantees.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data Quality &amp; Replacement</h2>
  <p>
    Every delivery is verified before it reaches you, and comes with our replacement guarantee.
    Full details — including what qualifies for a replacement and how to request one — are in our{' '}
    <a href="/refund-replacement-policy">Refund &amp; Replacement Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>
  <p>
    LeadVault provides data and campaign services for legitimate B2B outreach only. You agree not to
    use any dataset or service we provide to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Send deceptive, fraudulent, or misleading communications;</li>
    <li>Violate CAN-SPAM, applicable anti-spam laws, or any other law in the jurisdictions you contact;</li>
    <li>Harass, defraud, or knowingly target individuals who have opted out of contact; or</li>
    <li>Resell, redistribute, or sublicense a dataset we deliver to you, in whole or in part, without our prior written consent.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We reserve the right to decline any order, or to stop work on an active engagement, that we
    reasonably believe is intended for a use described above.
  </p>

  <h2>License to Delivered Data</h2>
  <p>
    When you purchase a dataset from LeadVault, we grant you a non-exclusive license to use it for
    your own business's outreach, sales, and marketing purposes. Ownership of the underlying data
    about third-party businesses and individuals is not transferred to you, and the license does not
    include the right to resell, sublicense, or redistribute the dataset itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    You may cancel a monthly subscription at any time; cancellation takes effect at the end of the
    current billing cycle, and we don't provide partial refunds for time already paid for in that
    cycle. To cancel, contact us using the details below.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    Data we source reflects information available at the time of verification; individuals and
    businesses change roles, contact details, and circumstances after delivery, and we can't
    guarantee results (response rates, conversions, or sales) from any dataset or campaign. Our
    services are provided "as is," and — other than the express replacement guarantee described in
    our Refund &amp; Replacement Policy — without other warranties, express or implied, to the
    fullest extent permitted by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, LeadVault's total liability arising out of any order or
    engagement is limited to the amount you paid for that specific order. We are not liable for
    indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, including lost profits, arising from your use
    of our data or services.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
  <p>
    The leadvaultdata.com website — its design, text, graphics, and the LeadVault name and logo —
    is owned by LeadVault and may not be copied or reused without our written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing Law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of Nigeria, without regard to conflict-of-law principles,
    without limiting any consumer-protection rights you may have under the law of your own
    jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use of the site or our services after a
    change means you accept the updated Terms. The "Last updated" date above reflects the most
    recent revision.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or
    reach us on WhatsApp at {PHONE_DISPLAY}.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
